Debug configurations
  ok      F5 builds the active file as a module and stops at its breakpoints
  ok      F5 fills in the default debug configuration
  ok      Ctrl+F5 builds without debug information and runs the program
  ok      F5 rebuilds the program after it changed
  ok      F5 does not start debugging when the build fails
  ok      F5 debugs a program whose PROGRAM-ID differs from the file name
  ok      a program can CALL a module built beforehand
  no bug  breakpoints in a CALLed module are hit
  BUG?    F5 on a file in a sub-directory
  BUG?    F5 on a file whose name contains a space
  ok      the launch configuration snippet builds and debugs the active file
  ok      a launch configuration with only a type and a request gets the defaults
  ok      a launch configuration can build and debug an executable
  ok      an executable is debugged without cobcrun when useCobcrun is not given
  ok      arguments are passed to the program
  ok      environment variables are passed to the program
  BUG?    the program runs in a configured working directory
  ok      Ctrl+F5 with a launch configuration runs the program
  BUG?    a launch configuration with a fixed target builds that target
  BUG?    F5 without a build task nor a built program ends the session
